#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128918 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "5110af12-1d0a-5f7e-8a3b-626cc437c53e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6097" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128919 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "bd93891e-1f9f-51af-a5c2-4eb5ca1178d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6098" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128920 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "e51c2aa9-027b-5b23-bcaf-805804a8de9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6099" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45242f4d-4225-5667-a0e4-cc82a69c00b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328280} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf2214f-7fbc-5de0-bbd3-2d2d218167ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328281} {:answer/id #uuid "4d098a7e-d70f-5bc0-8921-26ca679de49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328282} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b954ca-bfb8-5f05-b794-e7483543c9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328283} {:answer/id #uuid "29d05e24-e551-5cbd-9c62-39c0227ffae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29d05e24-e551-5cbd-9c62-39c0227ffae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328284} :answer-field/id #uuid "75822314-1f35-54ad-af45-1e19b05d6edd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a914a731-2557-5830-aa4d-f86a434e3214" :question/math-academy-id "q-129549" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $x+y=u,$ $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{y}^{1+y}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{y}^{1+y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{y+1}+\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{y+1}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c6ed6e9-ce09-5ea5-bc32-6f1730b18ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328287} {:answer/id #uuid "2b50727a-c7f5-5196-85b1-c340bc220532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328288} {:answer/id #uuid "85e9e631-ccc6-5b2b-9d3a-6262b32beb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328289} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2b6e62-e0ac-501d-997f-ec9cd07c6ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328290} {:answer/id #uuid "fe96da0e-5eb2-577d-9db1-e3fccd12593c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe96da0e-5eb2-577d-9db1-e3fccd12593c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1867a25-3270-58fa-99ba-8cc80cf96a2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "456aeadb-1a82-5da8-9100-a3eab9dc8ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-129550" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47b59bc1-a2e3-51ff-a5f0-e8840e10e3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328294} {:answer/id #uuid "2a17e6de-212c-5c19-a087-c7127d5dd99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328295} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd52f9-d9bb-561c-82cc-7d3ff4953215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328296} {:answer/id #uuid "478dad29-8876-5cf2-8e53-eae1efe9d64b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328297} {:answer/id #uuid "edd04d7b-dedb-5fda-bed9-bdc414835e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47b59bc1-a2e3-51ff-a5f0-e8840e10e3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328294} :answer-field/id #uuid "40157fc0-c0fc-5196-8030-be76f4c42d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a687ad08-b4b5-5aee-9377-c64aedd03364" :question/math-academy-id "q-129644" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(2x+\\frac{8}{3})-(x+\\frac{1}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb505034-f07c-5969-8499-ba1888c68370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328301} {:answer/id #uuid "7b85eead-6ea4-5ffa-9dbf-05336f91eea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328302} {:answer/id #uuid "54d1cd5a-0eb6-58c9-a9be-42ccd1b1e77e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328303} {:answer/id #uuid "543cbf94-8e83-5ec0-907f-853cffec26f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328304} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fb6df7-a4fa-5012-a1ad-833472d48fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb505034-f07c-5969-8499-ba1888c68370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328301} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e57e113-8971-5956-b522-f72888d2a0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19c5efcf-01ef-5fbf-9f64-6c90653aec20" :question/math-academy-id "q-129645" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $xy=u,$ $\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{u}]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =[{e}^{x}-x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cc9376c-f595-5a24-9ea7-535552dcdc52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328308} {:answer/id #uuid "070fe14f-c904-500e-823c-e55e7b8d1a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328309} {:answer/id #uuid "f36ea682-9013-575a-aae0-e8b6d23fccf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328310} {:answer/id #uuid "e4692e33-fc62-5914-a8a2-37395d57dc51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328311} {:answer/id #uuid "409029ae-4dc8-5bf3-b5c8-87c74550a6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "409029ae-4dc8-5bf3-b5c8-87c74550a6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328312} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e863687-7514-571c-aa1f-454dea7fbfa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4e727bd-8fd5-54cc-b4fe-00c16c127b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37951" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{3y}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-1)}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-2)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad446f99-b842-5a1f-9781-495a0a9d2b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328315} {:answer/id #uuid "7422fa66-43e0-55d7-9168-7e88966ee1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328316} {:answer/id #uuid "597056b1-7272-5392-a083-d7781bb54a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328317} {:answer/id #uuid "072bd4be-d5ca-508b-bb03-7d6816e97526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328318} {:answer/id #uuid "5e90189e-2806-57a2-b52a-fd24ed9e16d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "597056b1-7272-5392-a083-d7781bb54a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328317} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd3d376-0519-52d1-9277-4a01bb672fba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81aee10d-0b2a-5edf-957e-80f23e4fc897" :question/math-academy-id "q-72130" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $1$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "179dede6-5b04-58bf-a1e7-21b80fd01fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328322} {:answer/id #uuid "5e409c45-1ccd-5923-a127-7664c2de19e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328323} {:answer/id #uuid "6400e3ab-6c70-5278-bfca-a0962f17e481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328324} {:answer/id #uuid "00abc4c9-f9b1-575b-8794-8874828aecc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328325} {:answer/id #uuid "30bd559f-9d08-5288-ad54-c9ae60b7a556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30bd559f-9d08-5288-ad54-c9ae60b7a556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328326} :answer-field/id #uuid "034ae56c-bed7-531e-8adb-eb0c1a952cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80bfbd6a-391f-520f-a0ad-dc736395685b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72175" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "363694f2-1fb0-5b9b-980f-d61fd9cd90ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328329} {:answer/id #uuid "56783d26-7ea9-58ce-bf49-c5ff3cf187f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328330} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6e613c-a3bf-5ef9-9620-12b3e1fab9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328331} {:answer/id #uuid "54156bc8-7316-55b1-9557-c9baa00594b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328332} {:answer/id #uuid "be383f3d-3dfb-5455-be08-5ad3592f092b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f6e613c-a3bf-5ef9-9620-12b3e1fab9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328331} :answer-field/id #uuid "8af86ba6-5b96-5391-bec4-a98d51d985ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3eb8c440-ada3-5253-b326-b8092210096c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72197" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51445954-0d02-57fe-befe-1600ffeed056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328336} {:answer/id #uuid "0470a115-cad7-5479-85e1-cce013f00e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328337} {:answer/id #uuid "7b73bf84-6512-598d-bbd2-a0dbb36a6c80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328338} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cf1930-a260-5691-9779-acf4636e844d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328339} {:answer/id #uuid "98762fed-4d43-595e-b2fb-0686e391000a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7cf1930-a260-5691-9779-acf4636e844d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328339} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cdf5993-5f63-5411-abaa-bfdd4653edbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31325216-3d29-50c0-9808-63f126bc97f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-72264" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{e}^{xy}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{1\\cdot y}-{e}^{0\\cdot y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y}-y]_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =({e}^{4}-4)-({e}^{0}-0)\\text{ } \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-4-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68f8bc5-7807-577b-86fd-c9f7ef986aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}+e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328343} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa4efda-8a77-5084-89df-bcfb29035295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328344} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc1a623-857c-53ad-a2db-9d1d6b81fd80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}+e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328345} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe34107-b4fd-5b4b-9098-ad46a65022e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}-e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328346} {:answer/id #uuid "97ff462d-b1a7-56c8-95df-3d44d80c4291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3aa4efda-8a77-5084-89df-bcfb29035295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328344} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f30f112-94db-5290-8ef2-bd50992d56cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f26cd789-ba52-54de-bbae-2bbc2a46c9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72267" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{e}^{x+y}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{0+y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(e{e}^{y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y & =(e-1)[{e}^{y}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f068f0ef-25d5-5d1a-91f1-e53e594733bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328350} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0cb47f-7864-5275-9ef6-ebe404085f24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328351} {:answer/id #uuid "473ef58a-aede-537e-abbb-0ea50eef2b83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328352} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb245f5-1151-536f-9a8f-7dbfa203ecef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328353} {:answer/id #uuid "a5382880-63f0-50b0-b377-c1a56ac355f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfb245f5-1151-536f-9a8f-7dbfa203ecef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328353} :answer-field/id #uuid "2160c74f-18e4-5bd0-9363-acbce1ea89ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "293ef1c7-f62c-513e-bea6-e158b705aac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-72268" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(1-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =-2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c9d934-dee0-5e45-8999-42c192435238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328357} {:answer/id #uuid "931a8630-ae95-5f6e-8989-ed07faa969f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328358} {:answer/id #uuid "652d3777-5b3b-54fa-8534-6384fcccf2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328359} {:answer/id #uuid "210c9732-2e73-5c0c-99cd-1fd5efcd5e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328360} {:answer/id #uuid "654ca27c-0edf-5431-a2ba-0d0da5b6a933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931a8630-ae95-5f6e-8989-ed07faa969f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328358} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a122284-d8dd-5afb-9e25-bbe993f43898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d75c934-4b2e-5a66-8cae-88fc5a6df561" :question/math-academy-id "q-73578" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}(-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f0322a-06f2-5fdd-a36b-05129c510cb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328364} {:answer/id #uuid "dade62a3-48de-5fc8-bcca-93569ec08e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328365} {:answer/id #uuid "7efda17f-b0b1-5dc4-a8ac-9f1416cc2781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328366} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e8d490-3834-5524-8a93-33e222d82b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328367} {:answer/id #uuid "02b37091-4db1-5ec6-bc07-80cfa2dc04b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f0322a-06f2-5fdd-a36b-05129c510cb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328364} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46b802f-d1d4-5766-9163-99f5fb42ea26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61b00e5d-d3ee-52de-a72c-6ea3af391d5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73583" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{(1+(3x)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{12y}]}_{1/3}^{1/4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}}+\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48da782e-1f01-5787-b567-1aec6beadae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328371} {:answer/id #uuid "1e271abf-7e5d-5812-ad35-efb60b33d6f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328372} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6df562-353d-56c8-9046-266d639596bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328373} {:answer/id #uuid "5b610e08-51d9-537a-9828-e333bc48d53e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328374} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd37fd1-889a-5414-bb5f-a7b4dc45bb24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd37fd1-889a-5414-bb5f-a7b4dc45bb24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328375} :answer-field/id #uuid "015b846b-627f-5ee3-bb95-1b1b2cacc931" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84e85edf-4c2e-5a0c-ab98-f77929dd94e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73591" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{2}\\le x\\le {e}^{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{6}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{3}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}((\\sqrt[3]{6})^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c794778d-d6a8-5ca4-b34b-99a57dec5677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328378} {:answer/id #uuid "c84cf251-b895-5499-9ab1-deaba449235c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328379} {:answer/id #uuid "46d53d8e-95e7-59b1-81ca-034ea68d39d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328380} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7c1d00-a2ef-5bea-b85a-0a5d489f8b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328381} {:answer/id #uuid "956aba47-a7f4-5829-9b40-c75f7f783f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c794778d-d6a8-5ca4-b34b-99a57dec5677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328378} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b4ebdd-4a5c-579a-8412-a14370d6b40a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f11f8b7c-36a0-5fac-8519-f4d43bfce23c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73601" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(3+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{{3}^{1}-{3}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
